course: dictionary
lesson: 15769
title: Tucked, tucked in and tucked away
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: «Mum tucked the blanket around me.» Tucked means pushed the edges neatly in, so the blanket stays snug. The word around tells you the blanket is wrapped round you, so it is not thrown on or dropped.
explain: «Ravi tucked his shirt into his school trousers.» Tucked means pushed the edge of something neatly into or under something else. Try the swap test: put «pushed in» in place of tucked and read the sentence again. It still makes sense, so you know your meaning fits.
explain: «The little cottage was tucked away at the end of a quiet lane.» Tucked away means hidden, in a place that is hard to find. The clues are quiet lane and at the end, which tell you the cottage is not easy to spot.
explain: Tucked is also a verb, so it changes: tuck, tucks, tucking, tucked. Watch the small words after it, like in, away or into, because they change the meaning.
fact: Tucked means pushed the edge of something neatly into or under something else.
fact: «Tucked in» means cosy in bed, with the covers pushed in around you.
fact: «Tucked away» means hidden or in a quiet place that is hard to find.
fact: «Tuck in!» is what someone says to start eating, and «tucked in» can mean ate eagerly.
fact: For safety, tuck in loose clothes, laces and long hair when you are near bikes, machines and fires.
exercise: «Sam tucked his shirt into his school trousers.» What does tucked mean here? | *Pushed the edge in neatly | Threw it away in the bin | Washed it in the sink | Ironed it flat on the table
exercise: «The little cottage was tucked away at the end of a quiet lane.» What does tucked away mean? | Next to the busy shops | Painted bright red | *Hidden, in a place that is hard to find | Sold to a new family
exercise: Mum says, «Time to get tucked in.» What is going to happen? | *Getting into bed with the covers pushed in around you | Tidying your bedroom | Going out to play in the park | Eating your dinner in a hurry
test: Dad calls out, «Tuck in, everyone!» and the family starts eating. What does tuck in mean here? | Stop talking and sit quietly | Clean the table | *Start eating eagerly | Go to bed early
test: Ella puts a note «tucked in her pocket» so she will not lose it. What does tucked mean here? | Thrown away | *Put in a small safe place | Read aloud to the class | Torn into tiny pieces
exam: Before you ride your bike, make sure your laces are ___. | *Tucked in | Lost | Painted | Shouted
